      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-23T13:07:25Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-23T13:09:17Z",
      "duration_ms": 112000,
      "summary": [
        "Modified UpdateReferenceWithConfirmationAsync() in DiffDialogViewModel.cs to build a risk-aware confirmation message instead of the generic ConfirmUpdateMessage. When removed mods are present, the singular (count == 1 → ConfirmRiskyDetail_RemovedSingular) or plural (count > 1 → string.Format(ConfirmRiskyDetail_Removals, count)) detail line is assembled. Same pattern for inserted mods via ConfirmRiskyDetail_InsertedSingular / ConfirmRiskyDetail_Insertions. Both detail lines are joined with '\\n' into a detail block, then embedded into ConfirmUpdateMessage_RiskyChanges via string.Format({0}). The ConfirmationRequestedEventArgs now receives this composed message. ConfirmUpdateTitle and ConfirmationIcon.Warning remain unchanged. Safe-only paths (added/replaced mods only) do not enter the if-block at all, preserving the existing behavior of skipping the dialog entirely. Build: 0 errors, 0 warnings. 492/494 tests pass; 2 are intentionally skipped stubs (ConfirmationMessage_RiskyChanges_IncludesRemovedCount, ConfirmationMessage_SafeChanges_SkipsDialog) that document a known test-environment barrier for this method."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "ViewModels/DiffDialogViewModel.cs"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T13:09:17Z",
          "note": "UpdateReferenceWithConfirmationAsync() now uses System.Collections.Generic.List<string> with the fully-qualified namespace inline rather than a using directive, since the List<string> is local and does not appear elsewhere in the file. This is acceptable but a using alias or var with collection initializer could be slightly cleaner. Not a blocking issue."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T13:09:17Z",
          "note": "The two confirmation dialog unit tests (ConfirmationMessage_RiskyChanges_IncludesRemovedCount, ConfirmationMessage_SafeChanges_SkipsDialog) remain as skip-documented stubs in DiffDialogViewModelTests.cs. These tests cannot reach UpdateReferenceWithConfirmationAsync() because the test-only constructor wires UpdateReferenceCommand as a no-op stub. The logic is correct and observable at runtime, but unit-test coverage of the new message composition path is structurally blocked by the production constructor's MainViewModel dependency. A future refactoring to inject the message-building logic (or mock UpdateReferenceCommand via an interface) would unblock these tests."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T13:09:17Z",
          "note": "No other code in DiffDialogViewModel.cs required changes — the existing removedMods/insertedMods variables and the hasRemovedMods || hasInsertedMods conditional were already in place and required no restructuring. The change is minimal and well-contained."
        }
      ]
    },
